stages of Christianity's expansion. Though traditionally associated with Sicily as his place of origin (circa 50 CE), his enduring legacy is firmly anchored in what would become northern Portugal, where he is revered as a significant figure in the establishment and early development of the Christian faith. His life, concluding around 135 CE, falls squarely within the Classical Era, a time when the Roman Empire's vast administrative network inadvertently facilitated the transmission of new religious ideas, laying groundwork for future spiritual communities.

